// Tags defined in the data (design v23 §3.5.6). A contact is a sprite
// touching a thing: eating it, hitting it, playing with it, or crashing into
// it. A tag says what each contact with a thing that has it does to the sprite
// making it, and every thing with the tag behaves the same way. An object type
// names its tags in `objects.ron`, after the built-in Solid and Fixture.
//
// Each tag has:
//   name     what object types call it
//   contact  for each contact (Eat, Hit, Play, Crash), its effects, run before
//            the thing's own verb table. Only Inject and Signal on the Actor,
//            the sprite making contact, are allowed
[
    (name: "Thorny",
     contact: {
         Eat:   [Inject(Actor, "injury", 0.05), Signal(Actor, "pricked")],
         Hit:   [Inject(Actor, "injury", 0.03), Signal(Actor, "pricked")],
         Play:  [Inject(Actor, "injury", 0.03), Signal(Actor, "pricked")],
         Crash: [Inject(Actor, "injury", 0.03), Signal(Actor, "pricked")],
     }),
]
